---
title: Meringue lemon pie
category: Desserts
diet:
  - vegetarian
servings: 8
difficulty: average
prep time: 30 minutes
cook time: 35 minutes
created: 2026-05-21
updated: 2026-05-21
---

= Crust

Combine @flour{185%g}, @sugar{2%tsp}, and @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp} in a #food processor{}.

Add @unsalted butter{115%g}(chilled) and pulse to break it apart.

With the food processor running on low, pour in @water{2.5%Tbsp}(chilled). After about ~{10%seconds} it should start to look sticky while remaining crumbly enough.

Turn dough on a work surface and form into a ball.

Cover with plastic wrap and leave it to set in the refrigerator for ~{30%minutes}.

Take the dough from the refrigerator and roll it out on a floured surface with the help of a #rolling pin{}.

Transfer to a 23 cm pie pan and trim the dough around the edges. Make sure to leave 1 cm excess as the crust will shrink during baking.

Using a fork, poke holes into the bottom of the crust to prevent air pockets. Cover with parchment paper and fill the crust with pie weights.

> You can use dry rice or beans to weigh down the crust.

With the oven preheated to 190°C (170°C ventilated), blind bake for ~{15%minutes}.

Remove pie weighs and return to the oven for another ~{5%minutes}.

= Filling

In a bowl whisk together @condensed milk{400%g}, @egg yolks{4}, @lemon zest{1%lemon}, and @lemon juice{120%ml}.

Pour the mixture into the prepared pie crust.

= Meringue

Put @egg whites{4} and @cream of tartar{1/4%tsp} in a bowl and whisk until frothy. Add @caster sugar{6%Tbsp} and whisk until firm glossy peaks form.

Gently spread or pipe the meringue over the filling. Make sure the meringue touches the edges of the crust to prevent it from shrinking.

Bake for about ~{20%minutes} until the meringue is lightly browned.

Allow the pie to cool down before serving.